{"title_zh":"四大发明","subtitle_zh":"造纸术·印刷术·指南针·火药","title_en":"The Four Great Inventions","subtitle_en":"Paper · Printing · The Compass · Gunpowder","author":"Text and translation by Claude (Anthropic)","type":"meta"}
{"type":"p","id":"intro","segs":[{"en":"Almost every student in China has heard of the “Four Great Inventions”: papermaking, printing, the compass and gunpowder.","tok":[["在","zài"],["中国","Zhōngguó"],"，",["几乎","jīhū"],["每","měi"],["个","gè"],["学生","xuésheng"],["都","dōu"],["听说","tīngshuō"],["过","guo"],"“",["四大发明","sì dà fāmíng","Four Great Inventions","J"],"”","：",["造纸术","zàozhǐshù","papermaking","J"],"、",["印刷术","yìnshuāshù","printing","J"],"、",["指南针","zhǐnánzhēn","compass","J"],["和","hé"],["火药","huǒyào","gunpowder","J"],"。"]},{"en":"All four technologies first appeared in China long ago and later slowly spread to other parts of the world.","tok":[["这","zhè"],["四","sì"],["种","zhǒng"],["技术","jìshù"],["都","dōu"],["是","shì"],["很","hěn"],["早","zǎo"],["以前","yǐqián"],["在","zài"],["中国","Zhōngguó"],["出现","chūxiàn"],["的","de"],"，",["后来","hòulái"],["又","yòu"],["慢慢","mànmàn"],["传","chuán"],["到","dào"],["了","le"],["世界","shìjiè"],["上","shàng"],["别的","biéde"],["地方","dìfang"],"。"]},{"en":"They changed the way people wrote, read, travelled and fought wars, and they changed history too.","tok":[["它们","tāmen"],["改变","gǎibiàn"],["了","le"],["人们","rénmen"],["写字","xiězì"],"、",["读书","dúshū"],"、",["旅行","lǚxíng"],["和","hé"],["打仗","dǎzhàng","to fight a war"],["的","de"],["方法","fāngfǎ"],"，",["也","yě"],["改变","gǎibiàn"],["了","le"],["历史","lìshǐ"],"。"]},{"en":"Let us look at their stories one by one.","tok":[["下面","xiàmiàn"],["我们","wǒmen"],["就","jiù"],["一","yī"],["个","gè"],["一","yī"],["个","gè"],["地","de"],["来","lái"],["看看","kànkan"],["它们","tāmen"],["的","de"],["故事","gùshi"],"。"]}],"zh":"在中国，几乎每个学生都听说过“四大发明”：造纸术、印刷术、指南针和火药。这四种技术都是很早以前在中国出现的，后来又慢慢传到了世界上别的地方。它们改变了人们写字、读书、旅行和打仗的方法，也改变了历史。下面我们就一个一个地来看看它们的故事。"}
{"type":"h2","id":"h-paper","segs":[{"en":"Papermaking","tok":[["造纸术","zàozhǐshù","papermaking","J"]]}],"zh":"造纸术"}
{"type":"p","id":"paper-1","segs":[{"en":"Before paper appeared, what did Chinese people write on?","tok":[["在","zài"],["纸","zhǐ"],["出现","chūxiàn"],["以前","yǐqián"],"，",["中国","Zhōngguó"],["人","rén"],["把","bǎ"],["字","zì"],["写","xiě"],["在","zài"],["什么","shénme"],["上面","shàngmiàn"],["呢","ne"],"？"]},{"en":"The most common material was bamboo slips: bamboo cut into long, narrow strips and then tied together with cord.","tok":[["最","zuì"],["常用","chángyòng"],["的","de"],["是","shì"],["竹简","zhújiǎn","bamboo slips (for writing)","J"],"，",["就是","jiùshì"],["把","bǎ"],["竹子","zhúzi","bamboo"],["切","qiē"],["成","chéng"],["长长","chángcháng"],["的","de"],"、",["窄窄","zhǎizhǎi","narrow"],["的","de"],["片","piàn"],"，",["再","zài"],["用","yòng"],["绳子","shéngzi","string, cord"],["连","lián"],["在","zài"],["一起","yīqǐ"],"。"]},{"en":"Bamboo slips were heavy; a single book often had to be carried on a cart.","tok":[["竹简","zhújiǎn","bamboo slips (for writing)","J"],["很","hěn"],["重","zhòng"],"，",["一","yī"],["本","běn"],["书","shū"],["常常","chángcháng"],["要","yào"],["用","yòng"],["车","chē"],["来","lái"],["拉","lā"],"。"]},{"en":"The rich also wrote on silk, which is light and soft, but it was far too expensive for ordinary people.","tok":[["有钱人","yǒuqiánrén"],["也","yě"],["会","huì"],["在","zài"],["丝绸","sīchóu","silk"],["上","shàng"],["写字","xiězì"],"，",["丝绸","sīchóu","silk"],["又","yòu"],["轻","qīng"],["又","yòu"],["软","ruǎn","soft"],"，",["可是","kěshì"],["太","tài"],["贵","guì"],["了","le"],"，",["一般","yībān"],["人","rén"],["用不起","yòngbuqǐ","cannot afford to use"],"。"]}],"zh":"在纸出现以前，中国人把字写在什么上面呢？最常用的是竹简，就是把竹子切成长长的、窄窄的片，再用绳子连在一起。竹简很重，一本书常常要用车来拉。有钱人也会在丝绸上写字，丝绸又轻又软，可是太贵了，一般人用不起。"}
{"type":"p","id":"paper-2","segs":[{"en":"Archaeologists have found that as early as the Western Han, more than two thousand years ago, China already had a kind of coarse paper; but it was used mainly for wrapping things and was not very good for writing.","tok":[["考古学家","kǎogǔxuéjiā","archaeologist"],["发现","fāxiàn"],"，",["早","zǎo"],["在","zài"],["两千","liǎngqiān"],["多","duō"],["年","nián"],["前","qián"],["的","de"],["西汉","Xī Hàn","Western Han dynasty","N"],"，",["中国","Zhōngguó"],["就","jiù"],["已经","yǐjīng"],["有","yǒu"],["了","le"],["一","yī"],["种","zhǒng"],["很","hěn"],["粗","cū","coarse"],["的","de"],["纸","zhǐ"],"，",["不过","bùguò"],["当时","dāngshí"],["的","de"],["纸","zhǐ"],["主要","zhǔyào"],["用来","yònglái","to be used for"],["包","bāo"],["东西","dōngxi"],"，",["不","bù"],["太","tài"],["适合","shìhé"],["写字","xiězì"],"。"]},{"en":"In the Eastern Han, an official named Cai Lun improved the way paper was made.","tok":[["到","dào"],["了","le"],["东汉","Dōng Hàn","Eastern Han dynasty","N"],"，",["一","yī"],["位","wèi"],["叫","jiào"],["蔡伦","Cài Lún","Cai Lun, Eastern Han court official","N"],["的","de"],["官员","guānyuán","official"],["改进","gǎijìn","to improve"],["了","le"],["造纸","zàozhǐ","to make paper"],["的","de"],["方法","fāngfǎ"],"。"]},{"en":"It is said that around AD 105 he soaked tree bark, hemp, old cloth and worn-out fishing nets in water until they went soft, and then beat them into pulp.","tok":[["据说","jùshuō","it is said"],["在","zài"],["公元","gōngyuán","AD, Common Era"],"105",["年","nián"],["左右","zuǒyòu"],"，",["他","tā"],["把","bǎ"],["树皮","shùpí","tree bark"],"、",["麻","má","hemp"],"、",["旧","jiù"],["布","bù"],["和","hé"],["破","pò"],["渔网","yúwǎng","fishing net"],["放","fàng"],["在","zài"],["水","shuǐ"],["里","lǐ"],["泡","pào","to soak"],["烂","làn","to go soft"],"，",["再","zài"],["把","bǎ"],["它们","tāmen"],["打","dǎ"],["成","chéng"],["纸浆","zhǐjiāng","paper pulp","J"],"。"]},{"en":"Then a fine bamboo screen was used to lift the pulp out of the water; once the water had drained away, the pulp had become a thin sheet of paper.","tok":[["然后","ránhòu"],"，",["人们","rénmen"],["用","yòng"],["一","yī"],["张","zhāng"],["细细","xìxì"],["的","de"],["竹帘","zhúlián","bamboo screen","J"],["把","bǎ"],["纸浆","zhǐjiāng","paper pulp","J"],["从","cóng"],["水","shuǐ"],["里","lǐ"],["捞","lāo","to scoop up"],["起来","qǐlai"],"，",["等","děng"],["水","shuǐ"],["流","liú"],["走","zǒu"],"，",["纸浆","zhǐjiāng","paper pulp","J"],["就","jiù"],["变成","biànchéng"],["了","le"],["一","yī"],["层","céng"],["薄薄","báobáo","thin"],["的","de"],["纸","zhǐ"],"。"]},{"en":"This paper was light and cheap, and easy to write on, so it soon became popular all over the country.","tok":[["这种","zhèzhǒng"],["纸","zhǐ"],["又","yòu"],["轻","qīng"],["又","yòu"],["便宜","piányi"],"，",["写字","xiězì"],["也","yě"],["很","hěn"],["方便","fāngbiàn"],"，",["所以","suǒyǐ"],["很","hěn"],["快","kuài"],["就","jiù"],["在","zài"],["全国","quánguó"],["流行","liúxíng"],["起来","qǐlai"],"。"]}],"zh":"考古学家发现，早在两千多年前的西汉，中国就已经有了一种很粗的纸，不过当时的纸主要用来包东西，不太适合写字。到了东汉，一位叫蔡伦的官员改进了造纸的方法。据说在公元105年左右，他把树皮、麻、旧布和破渔网放在水里泡烂，再把它们打成纸浆。然后，人们用一张细细的竹帘把纸浆从水里捞起来，等水流走，纸浆就变成了一层薄薄的纸。这种纸又轻又便宜，写字也很方便，所以很快就在全国流行起来。"}
{"type":"p","id":"paper-3","segs":[{"en":"For a long time, only the Chinese knew how to make paper.","tok":[["很","hěn"],["长","cháng"],["一","yī"],["段","duàn"],["时间","shíjiān"],["里","lǐ"],"，",["造纸","zàozhǐ","to make paper"],["的","de"],["方法","fāngfǎ"],["只有","zhǐyǒu"],["中国","Zhōngguó"],["人","rén"],["知道","zhīdào"],"。"]},{"en":"Later the technique spread first to the Korean peninsula and Japan, and then westward along the Silk Road.","tok":[["后来","hòulái"],"，",["这种","zhèzhǒng"],["技术","jìshù"],["先","xiān"],["传","chuán"],["到","dào"],["了","le"],["朝鲜半岛","Cháoxiǎn Bàndǎo","Korean peninsula","N"],["和","hé"],["日本","Rìběn"],"，",["又","yòu"],["沿着","yánzhe","along"],["丝绸之路","Sīchóu zhī Lù","the Silk Road","N"],["向","xiàng"],["西","xī"],["传播","chuánbō","to spread"],"。"]},{"en":"It is said that after a battle in 751, some Chinese papermakers were taken to Samarkand in Central Asia; from there papermaking reached the Arab world, and several hundred years later Europe.","tok":[["据说","jùshuō","it is said"],["在","zài"],["公元","gōngyuán","AD, Common Era"],"751",["年","nián"],["的","de"],["一","yī"],["场","chǎng"],["战争","zhànzhēng"],["以后","yǐhòu"],"，",["一些","yīxiē"],["会","huì"],["造纸","zàozhǐ","to make paper"],["的","de"],["中国","Zhōngguó"],["工人","gōngrén"],["被","bèi"],["带","dài"],["到","dào"],["了","le"],["中亚","Zhōng Yà","Central Asia","N"],["的","de"],["撒马尔罕","Sāmǎ'ěrhǎn","Samarkand","N"],"，",["造纸术","zàozhǐshù","papermaking","J"],["从","cóng"],["那里","nàli"],["传","chuán"],["到","dào"],["了","le"],["阿拉伯","Ālābó","Arab, Arabia","N"],["世界","shìjiè"],"，",["几百","jǐbǎi"],["年","nián"],["以后","yǐhòu"],["又","yòu"],["到","dào"],["了","le"],["欧洲","Ōuzhōu","Europe"],"。"]},{"en":"With cheap paper, books became more and more common, and knowledge could be passed on to many more people.","tok":[["有","yǒu"],["了","le"],["便宜","piányi"],["的","de"],["纸","zhǐ"],"，",["书","shū"],["变得","biànde"],["越来越","yuèláiyuè"],["多","duō"],"，",["知识","zhīshi"],["也","yě"],["更","gèng"],["容易","róngyì"],["传","chuán"],["给","gěi"],["更","gèng"],["多","duō"],["的","de"],["人","rén"],"。"]}],"zh":"很长一段时间里，造纸的方法只有中国人知道。后来，这种技术先传到了朝鲜半岛和日本，又沿着丝绸之路向西传播。据说在公元751年的一场战争以后，一些会造纸的中国工人被带到了中亚的撒马尔罕，造纸术从那里传到了阿拉伯世界，几百年以后又到了欧洲。有了便宜的纸，书变得越来越多，知识也更容易传给更多的人。"}
{"type":"h2","id":"h-print","segs":[{"en":"Printing","tok":[["印刷术","yìnshuāshù","printing","J"]]}],"zh":"印刷术"}
{"type":"p","id":"print-1","segs":[{"en":"Once there was paper, a quick way of making books was still needed.","tok":[["有","yǒu"],["了","le"],["纸","zhǐ"],"，",["还","hái"],["需要","xūyào"],["一","yī"],["种","zhǒng"],["快速","kuàisù"],["做","zuò"],["书","shū"],["的","de"],["方法","fāngfǎ"],"。"]},{"en":"Before that, every book had to be copied by hand, character by character; copying one book took many days, and mistakes crept in easily.","tok":[["以前","yǐqián"],"，",["每","měi"],["一","yī"],["本","běn"],["书","shū"],["都","dōu"],["得","děi"],["用","yòng"],["手","shǒu"],["一","yī"],["个","gè"],["字","zì"],["一","yī"],["个","gè"],["字","zì"],["地","de"],["抄","chāo","to copy (by hand)"],"，",["抄","chāo","to copy (by hand)"],["一","yī"],["本","běn"],["书","shū"],["要","yào"],["花","huā"],["很多","hěnduō"],["天","tiān"],"，",["而且","érqiě"],["很","hěn"],["容易","róngyì"],["抄","chāo","to copy (by hand)"],["错","cuò"],"。"]},{"en":"Probably during the Tang dynasty, people invented woodblock printing.","tok":[["大概","dàgài"],["在","zài"],["唐代","Tángdài","Tang dynasty (618–907)","N"],"，",["人们","rénmen"],["发明","fāmíng"],["了","le"],["雕版印刷","diāobǎn yìnshuā","woodblock printing","J"],"。"]},{"en":"First they carved the text of a whole page, in reverse, into a wooden block; then they brushed ink onto the block, laid paper on top and pressed it gently, and the page was printed.","tok":[["他们","tāmen"],["先","xiān"],["把","bǎ"],["一","yī"],["页","yè"],["书","shū"],["的","de"],["内容","nèiróng"],["反","fǎn"],["着","zhe"],["刻","kè","to carve"],["在","zài"],["一","yī"],["块","kuài"],["木板","mùbǎn","wooden board"],["上","shàng"],"，",["然后","ránhòu"],["在","zài"],["木板","mùbǎn","wooden board"],["上","shàng"],["刷","shuā","to brush"],["上","shàng"],["墨","mò","ink"],"，",["再","zài"],["把","bǎ"],["纸","zhǐ"],["放","fàng"],["上去","shàngqù"],["轻轻","qīngqīng"],["地","de"],["压","yā","to press"],"，",["一","yī"],["页","yè"],["书","shū"],["就","jiù"],["印","yìn","to print"],["好","hǎo"],["了","le"],"。"]},{"en":"The same block could be printed again and again, so hundreds or thousands of copies of a book could be made.","tok":[["同","tóng","same"],["一","yī"],["块","kuài"],["木板","mùbǎn","wooden board"],["可以","kěyǐ"],["印","yìn","to print"],["很多","hěnduō"],["次","cì"],"，",["所以","suǒyǐ"],["一","yī"],["本","běn"],["书","shū"],["可以","kěyǐ"],["印","yìn","to print"],["出","chū"],["成百上千","chéngbǎi shàngqiān","hundreds or thousands","I"],["份","fèn"],"。"]}],"zh":"有了纸，还需要一种快速做书的方法。以前，每一本书都得用手一个字一个字地抄，抄一本书要花很多天，而且很容易抄错。大概在唐代，人们发明了雕版印刷。他们先把一页书的内容反着刻在一块木板上，然后在木板上刷上墨，再把纸放上去轻轻地压，一页书就印好了。同一块木板可以印很多次，所以一本书可以印出成百上千份。"}
{"type":"p","id":"print-2","segs":[{"en":"The oldest surviving printed book with a clear date is a Tang-dynasty copy of the Diamond Sutra; the date on it corresponds to the year 868.","tok":[["现在","xiànzài"],["能","néng"],["看到","kàndào"],["的","de"],"、",["最","zuì"],["早","zǎo"],["的","de"],"、",["有","yǒu"],["明确","míngquè","clear, definite"],["日期","rìqī"],["的","de"],["印刷","yìnshuā","to print"],["书","shū"],"，",["是","shì"],["一","yī"],["本","běn"],["唐代","Tángdài","Tang dynasty (618–907)","N"],["的","de"],"《",["金刚经","Jīngāng Jīng","the Diamond Sutra (Buddhist text)","N"],"》","，",["上面","shàngmiàn"],["的","de"],["日期","rìqī"],["相当于","xiāngdāngyú","to be equivalent to"],["公元","gōngyuán","AD, Common Era"],"868",["年","nián"],"。"]},{"en":"It was found in a cave at Dunhuang and is kept today in the British Library in London.","tok":[["这","zhè"],["本","běn"],["书","shū"],["是","shì"],["在","zài"],["敦煌","Dūnhuáng","Dunhuang (oasis town in Gansu)","N"],["的","de"],["一","yī"],["个","gè"],["山洞","shāndòng","cave"],["里","lǐ"],["发现","fāxiàn"],["的","de"],"，",["今天","jīntiān"],["保存","bǎocún"],["在","zài"],["英国","Yīngguó"],["伦敦","Lúndūn","London","N"],["的","de"],["大英图书馆","Dàyīng Túshūguǎn","the British Library","N"],["里","lǐ"],"。"]},{"en":"Woodblock printing had a drawback, though: every new book needed a whole new set of carved blocks, which cost a great deal of time and effort.","tok":[["不过","bùguò"],"，",["雕版印刷","diāobǎn yìnshuā","woodblock printing","J"],["也","yě"],["有","yǒu"],["缺点","quēdiǎn"],"：",["每","měi"],["印","yìn","to print"],["一","yī"],["本","běn"],["新","xīn"],["书","shū"],"，",["都","dōu"],["要","yào"],["刻","kè","to carve"],["一","yī"],["套","tào"],["新","xīn"],["的","de"],["木板","mùbǎn","wooden board"],"，",["又","yòu"],["费","fèi","to use up, to cost"],["时间","shíjiān"],["又","yòu"],["费","fèi","to use up, to cost"],["力气","lìqi"],"。"]}],"zh":"现在能看到的、最早的、有明确日期的印刷书，是一本唐代的《金刚经》，上面的日期相当于公元868年。这本书是在敦煌的一个山洞里发现的，今天保存在英国伦敦的大英图书馆里。不过，雕版印刷也有缺点：每印一本新书，都要刻一套新的木板，又费时间又费力气。"}
{"type":"p","id":"print-3","segs":[{"en":"In the Northern Song, an ordinary craftsman named Bi Sheng came up with a new idea.","tok":[["到","dào"],["了","le"],["北宋","Běi Sòng","Northern Song dynasty (960–1127)","N"],"，",["一","yī"],["个","gè"],["叫","jiào"],["毕昇","Bì Shēng","Bi Sheng, 11th-century inventor of movable type","N"],["的","de"],["普通","pǔtōng"],["工匠","gōngjiàng","craftsman"],["想","xiǎng"],["出","chū"],["了","le"],["一","yī"],["个","gè"],["新","xīn"],["办法","bànfǎ"],"。"]},{"en":"He made many small blocks of clay, carved one character on each, and then hardened them in a fire: this was movable type.","tok":[["他","tā"],["用","yòng"],["黏土","niántǔ","clay"],["做成","zuòchéng"],["很多","hěnduō"],["小","xiǎo"],["方块","fāngkuài","small square block"],"，",["每","měi"],["个","gè"],["方块","fāngkuài","small square block"],["上","shàng"],["刻","kè","to carve"],["一","yī"],["个","gè"],["字","zì"],"，",["然后","ránhòu"],["用","yòng"],["火","huǒ"],["烧","shāo"],["硬","yìng","hard"],"，",["这","zhè"],["就是","jiùshì"],["活字","huózì","movable type","J"],"。"]},{"en":"To print, the characters needed were set one by one on an iron plate; after printing, the type could be taken apart and used again next time.","tok":[["印","yìn","to print"],["书","shū"],["的","de"],["时候","shíhou"],"，",["把","bǎ"],["需要","xūyào"],["的","de"],["字","zì"],["一","yī"],["个","gè"],["一","yī"],["个","gè"],["排","pái","to arrange"],["在","zài"],["铁板","tiěbǎn","iron plate"],["上","shàng"],"，",["印","yìn","to print"],["完","wán"],["以后","yǐhòu"],"，",["还","hái"],["可以","kěyǐ"],["把","bǎ"],["字","zì"],["拆","chāi","to take apart"],["下来","xiàlai"],"，",["下次","xiàcì"],["再","zài"],["用","yòng"],"。"]},{"en":"Bi Sheng's story was written down by the Song scholar Shen Kuo in his Dream Pool Essays; that is the only reason we know about it today.","tok":[["毕昇","Bì Shēng","Bi Sheng, 11th-century inventor of movable type","N"],["的","de"],["故事","gùshi"],["被","bèi"],["宋代","Sòngdài","Song dynasty","N"],["的","de"],["学者","xuézhě","scholar"],["沈括","Shěn Kuò","Shen Kuo (1031–1095), Song scholar","N"],["记","jì"],["在","zài"],["了","le"],["他","tā"],["的","de"],"《",["梦溪笔谈","Mèngxī Bǐtán","Dream Pool Essays, Shen Kuo's notebook","N"],"》",["里","lǐ"],"，",["所以","suǒyǐ"],["我们","wǒmen"],["今天","jīntiān"],["才","cái"],["能","néng"],["知道","zhīdào"],"。"]}],"zh":"到了北宋，一个叫毕昇的普通工匠想出了一个新办法。他用黏土做成很多小方块，每个方块上刻一个字，然后用火烧硬，这就是活字。印书的时候，把需要的字一个一个排在铁板上，印完以后，还可以把字拆下来，下次再用。毕昇的故事被宋代的学者沈括记在了他的《梦溪笔谈》里，所以我们今天才能知道。"}
{"type":"p","id":"print-4","segs":[{"en":"But Chinese has a huge number of characters: a set of type needed thousands or even tens of thousands of pieces, so in China woodblock printing always remained more common than movable type.","tok":[["但是","dànshì"],"，",["汉字","Hànzì"],["的","de"],["数量","shùliàng"],["非常","fēicháng"],["多","duō"],"，",["一","yī"],["套","tào"],["活字","huózì","movable type","J"],["要","yào"],["准备","zhǔnbèi"],["几千","jǐqiān"],["个","gè"],["甚至","shènzhì"],["几万","jǐwàn"],["个","gè"],["字","zì"],"，",["所以","suǒyǐ"],["在","zài"],["中国","Zhōngguó"],"，",["雕版印刷","diāobǎn yìnshuā","woodblock printing","J"],["一直","yīzhí"],["用","yòng"],["得","de"],["比","bǐ"],["活字","huózì","movable type","J"],["更","gèng"],["多","duō"],"。"]},{"en":"Later, type was also made of wood and of metal, and the Korean peninsula was an early user of metal type.","tok":[["后来","hòulái"],"，",["人们","rénmen"],["又","yòu"],["用","yòng"],["木头","mùtou"],["和","hé"],["金属","jīnshǔ","metal"],["做","zuò"],["活字","huózì","movable type","J"],"，",["朝鲜半岛","Cháoxiǎn Bàndǎo","Korean peninsula","N"],["也","yě"],["很","hěn"],["早","zǎo"],["就","jiù"],["用","yòng"],["上","shàng"],["了","le"],["金属","jīnshǔ","metal"],["活字","huózì","movable type","J"],"。"]},{"en":"About four hundred years later, the German Gutenberg built a metal movable-type printing press in Europe.","tok":[["大约","dàyuē"],["四百","sìbǎi"],["年","nián"],["以后","yǐhòu"],"，",["德国","Déguó","Germany"],["人","rén"],["古腾堡","Gǔténgbǎo","Johannes Gutenberg (c. 1400–1468)","N"],["在","zài"],["欧洲","Ōuzhōu","Europe"],["做","zuò"],["出","chū"],["了","le"],["金属","jīnshǔ","metal"],["活字","huózì","movable type","J"],["印刷机","yìnshuājī","printing press","J"],"。"]},{"en":"Whether he was influenced by China is something historians still discuss today.","tok":[["他","tā"],["是","shì"],["不","bù"],["是","shì"],["受到","shòudào"],["了","le"],["中国","Zhōngguó"],["的","de"],["影响","yǐngxiǎng"],"，",["历史学家","lìshǐxuéjiā","historian"],["到","dào"],["今天","jīntiān"],["还","hái"],["在","zài"],["讨论","tǎolùn"],"。"]},{"en":"Either way, printing made books cheap and gave many more ordinary people the chance to read.","tok":[["不管","bùguǎn"],["怎么样","zěnmeyàng"],"，",["印刷术","yìnshuāshù","printing","J"],["让","ràng"],["书","shū"],["变得","biànde"],["便宜","piányi"],"，",["让","ràng"],["更","gèng"],["多","duō"],["的","de"],["普通","pǔtōng"],["人","rén"],["有","yǒu"],["机会","jīhuì"],["读书","dúshū"],"。"]}],"zh":"但是，汉字的数量非常多，一套活字要准备几千个甚至几万个字，所以在中国，雕版印刷一直用得比活字更多。后来，人们又用木头和金属做活字，朝鲜半岛也很早就用上了金属活字。大约四百年以后，德国人古腾堡在欧洲做出了金属活字印刷机。他是不是受到了中国的影响，历史学家到今天还在讨论。不管怎么样，印刷术让书变得便宜，让更多的普通人有机会读书。"}
{"type":"h2","id":"h-compass","segs":[{"en":"The Compass","tok":[["指南针","zhǐnánzhēn","compass","J"]]}],"zh":"指南针"}
{"type":"p","id":"compass-1","segs":[{"en":"Long ago, the Chinese discovered a strange kind of stone that could hold on to iron: the lodestone.","tok":[["很","hěn"],["早","zǎo"],["以前","yǐqián"],"，",["中国","Zhōngguó"],["人","rén"],["就","jiù"],["发现","fāxiàn"],["了","le"],["一","yī"],["种","zhǒng"],["奇怪","qíguài"],["的","de"],["石头","shítou"],"，",["它","tā"],["能","néng"],["吸","xī","to attract"],["住","zhù"],["铁","tiě"],"，",["这","zhè"],["就是","jiùshì"],["磁石","císhí","lodestone, magnet","J"],"。"]},{"en":"According to ancient books, more than two thousand years ago there was already a device called the sinan, the “south-pointer”.","tok":[["根据","gēnjù"],["古","gǔ"],["书","shū"],["的","de"],["记载","jìzǎi","record, account"],"，",["两千","liǎngqiān"],["多","duō"],["年","nián"],["前","qián"],["已经","yǐjīng"],["有","yǒu"],["了","le"],["一","yī"],["种","zhǒng"],["叫","jiào"],"“",["司南","sīnán","sinan, ancient “south-pointer”","J"],"”",["的","de"],["东西","dōngxi"],"。"]},{"en":"It was a spoon made of lodestone, placed on a smooth plate; once spun, the spoon would come to rest with its handle pointing south.","tok":[["它","tā"],["是","shì"],["用","yòng"],["磁石","císhí","lodestone, magnet","J"],["做成","zuòchéng"],["的","de"],["勺子","sháozi","spoon"],"，",["放","fàng"],["在","zài"],["一","yī"],["个","gè"],["光滑","guānghuá","smooth"],["的","de"],["盘子","pánzi"],["上","shàng"],"，",["转动","zhuǎndòng","to turn, to spin"],["以后","yǐhòu"],"，",["勺子","sháozi","spoon"],["的","de"],["把儿","bàr","handle"],["最后","zuìhòu"],["会","huì"],["指","zhǐ"],["向","xiàng"],["南方","nánfāng"],"。"]},{"en":"Scholars do not fully agree, however, on what the sinan really looked like or how it was used.","tok":[["不过","bùguò"],"，",["司南","sīnán","sinan, ancient “south-pointer”","J"],["到底","dàodǐ"],["是","shì"],["什么","shénme"],["样子","yàngzi"],"，",["怎么","zěnme"],["用","yòng"],"，",["学者","xuézhě","scholar"],["们","men"],["的","de"],["看法","kànfǎ"],["并","bìng"],["不","bù"],["完全","wánquán"],["一样","yīyàng"],"。"]}],"zh":"很早以前，中国人就发现了一种奇怪的石头，它能吸住铁，这就是磁石。根据古书的记载，两千多年前已经有了一种叫“司南”的东西。它是用磁石做成的勺子，放在一个光滑的盘子上，转动以后，勺子的把儿最后会指向南方。不过，司南到底是什么样子，怎么用，学者们的看法并不完全一样。"}
{"type":"p","id":"compass-2","segs":[{"en":"At first, such tools were used mainly for fengshui, for example to decide which way a house or a tomb should face.","tok":[["一","yī"],["开始","kāishǐ"],"，",["人们","rénmen"],["主要","zhǔyào"],["用","yòng"],["这种","zhèzhǒng"],["工具","gōngjù"],["来","lái"],["看","kàn"],["风水","fēngshuǐ","fengshui","J"],"，",["比如","bǐrú"],["决定","juédìng"],["房子","fángzi"],["和","hé"],["坟墓","fénmù","tomb, grave"],["的","de"],["方向","fāngxiàng"],"。"]},{"en":"By the Song dynasty, people had found that rubbing an iron needle with lodestone made the needle magnetic too, and far more sensitive than a spoon.","tok":[["到","dào"],["了","le"],["宋代","Sòngdài","Song dynasty","N"],"，",["人们","rénmen"],["发现","fāxiàn"],"，",["用","yòng"],["磁石","císhí","lodestone, magnet","J"],["摩擦","mócā","to rub"],["一","yī"],["根","gēn"],["铁","tiě"],["针","zhēn","needle"],"，",["铁","tiě"],["针","zhēn","needle"],["也","yě"],["会","huì"],["有","yǒu"],["磁性","cíxìng","magnetism","J"],"，",["而且","érqiě"],["比","bǐ"],["勺子","sháozi","spoon"],["灵敏","língmǐn","sensitive"],["得","de"],["多","duō"],"。"]},{"en":"Shen Kuo also wrote about such needles in his book, and recorded an important observation: the needle does not point due south, but slightly to one side.","tok":[["沈括","Shěn Kuò","Shen Kuo (1031–1095), Song scholar","N"],["在","zài"],["书","shū"],["里","lǐ"],["也","yě"],["写","xiě"],["到","dào"],["了","le"],["这种","zhèzhǒng"],["磁针","cízhēn","magnetic needle","J"],"，",["还","hái"],["记录","jìlù"],["了","le"],["一","yī"],["个","gè"],["重要","zhòngyào"],["的","de"],["发现","fāxiàn"],"：",["针","zhēn","needle"],["指","zhǐ"],["的","de"],["方向","fāngxiàng"],["并","bìng"],["不","bù"],["是","shì"],["正","zhèng"],["南","nán"],"，",["而是","érshì"],["稍微","shāowēi","slightly"],["偏","piān","to lean to one side"],["一点儿","yīdiǎnr"],"。"]},{"en":"By floating the needle on water or hanging it from a silk thread, people made a much handier compass.","tok":[["人们","rénmen"],["把","bǎ"],["针","zhēn","needle"],["放","fàng"],["在","zài"],["水","shuǐ"],["上","shàng"],["漂","piāo","to float"],["着","zhe"],"，",["或者","huòzhě"],["用","yòng"],["丝线","sīxiàn","silk thread"],["挂","guà"],["起来","qǐlai"],"，",["就","jiù"],["做成","zuòchéng"],["了","le"],["更","gèng"],["好用","hǎoyòng"],["的","de"],["指南针","zhǐnánzhēn","compass","J"],"。"]}],"zh":"一开始，人们主要用这种工具来看风水，比如决定房子和坟墓的方向。到了宋代，人们发现，用磁石摩擦一根铁针，铁针也会有磁性，而且比勺子灵敏得多。沈括在书里也写到了这种磁针，还记录了一个重要的发现：针指的方向并不是正南，而是稍微偏一点儿。人们把针放在水上漂着，或者用丝线挂起来，就做成了更好用的指南针。"}
{"type":"p","id":"compass-3","segs":[{"en":"The compass's most important use was at sea.","tok":[["指南针","zhǐnánzhēn","compass","J"],["最","zuì"],["重要","zhòngyào"],["的","de"],["用处","yòngchu","use"],["是","shì"],["在","zài"],["海","hǎi"],["上","shàng"],"。"]},{"en":"Out on the open sea, when the sky is overcast and neither the sun nor the stars can be seen, a ship easily loses its way.","tok":[["在","zài"],["大海","dàhǎi"],["上","shàng"],"，",["阴天","yīntiān"],["的","de"],["时候","shíhou"],["看不到","kànbudào"],["太阳","tàiyang"],["和","hé"],["星星","xīngxing"],"，",["船","chuán"],["很","hěn"],["容易","róngyì"],["迷路","mílù","to get lost"],"。"]},{"en":"By around the end of the Northern Song, Chinese sailors had already begun to use the compass to find their direction.","tok":[["大约","dàyuē"],["在","zài"],["北宋","Běi Sòng","Northern Song dynasty (960–1127)","N"],["末年","mònián","final years"],"，",["中国","Zhōngguó"],["的","de"],["船员","chuányuán","sailor, crew"],["已经","yǐjīng"],["开始","kāishǐ"],["用","yòng"],["指南针","zhǐnánzhēn","compass","J"],["来","lái"],["确定","quèdìng"],["方向","fāngxiàng"],["了","le"],"。"]},{"en":"Later, Arabs and Europeans began to use the compass as well.","tok":[["后来","hòulái"],"，",["阿拉伯","Ālābó","Arab, Arabia","N"],["人","rén"],["和","hé"],["欧洲","Ōuzhōu","Europe"],["人","rén"],["也","yě"],["用","yòng"],["上","shàng"],["了","le"],["指南针","zhǐnánzhēn","compass","J"],"。"]},{"en":"Without the compass, the great ocean voyages the Europeans later made would hardly have been possible, and the map of the world might look quite different.","tok":[["没有","méiyǒu"],["指南针","zhǐnánzhēn","compass","J"],"，",["后来","hòulái"],["欧洲","Ōuzhōu","Europe"],["人","rén"],["的","de"],["远洋","yuǎnyáng","ocean-going"],["航行","hángxíng","voyage, navigation"],["就","jiù"],["很","hěn"],["难","nán"],["实现","shíxiàn"],"，",["世界","shìjiè"],["地图","dìtú"],["也","yě"],["可能","kěnéng"],["会","huì"],["是","shì"],["另","lìng","another"],["一","yī"],["个","gè"],["样子","yàngzi"],"。"]}],"zh":"指南针最重要的用处是在海上。在大海上，阴天的时候看不到太阳和星星，船很容易迷路。大约在北宋末年，中国的船员已经开始用指南针来确定方向了。后来，阿拉伯人和欧洲人也用上了指南针。没有指南针，后来欧洲人的远洋航行就很难实现，世界地图也可能会是另一个样子。"}
{"type":"p","id":"compass-4","segs":[{"en":"In China, the Ming admiral Zheng He led a huge fleet on seven voyages to the “Western Oceans”, reaching as far as the east coast of Africa.","tok":[["在","zài"],["中国","Zhōngguó"],"，",["明代","Míngdài","Ming dynasty (1368–1644)","N"],["的","de"],["郑和","Zhèng Hé","Zheng He (1371–1433), Ming admiral","N"],["带","dài"],["着","zhe"],["很","hěn"],["大","dà"],["的","de"],["船队","chuánduì","fleet"],["七","qī"],["次","cì"],["下西洋","xià Xīyáng","to sail the “Western Oceans”","J"],"，",["最","zuì"],["远","yuǎn"],["到","dào"],["了","le"],["非洲","Fēizhōu","Africa","N"],["的","de"],["东","dōng"],["海岸","hǎi'àn","coast"],"。"]},{"en":"Their sea charts noted, for each stretch of the way, which compass direction to follow.","tok":[["他们","tāmen"],["的","de"],["航海图","hánghǎitú","nautical chart","J"],["上","shàng"],"，",["写","xiě"],["着","zhe"],["每","měi"],["一","yī"],["段","duàn"],["路","lù"],["应该","yīnggāi"],["按照","ànzhào"],["指南针","zhǐnánzhēn","compass","J"],["的","de"],["哪","nǎ"],["个","gè"],["方向","fāngxiàng"],["走","zǒu"],"。"]},{"en":"This way of recording a route was called a “needle route”.","tok":[["这种","zhèzhǒng"],["记录","jìlù"],["航线","hángxiàn","sea route","J"],["的","de"],["方法","fāngfǎ"],"，",["叫做","jiàozuò"],"“",["针路","zhēnlù","“needle route”, compass bearing","J"],"”","。"]}],"zh":"在中国，明代的郑和带着很大的船队七次下西洋，最远到了非洲的东海岸。他们的航海图上，写着每一段路应该按照指南针的哪个方向走。这种记录航线的方法，叫做“针路”。"}
{"type":"h2","id":"h-gunpowder","segs":[{"en":"Gunpowder","tok":[["火药","huǒyào","gunpowder","J"]]}],"zh":"火药"}
{"type":"p","id":"gp-1","segs":[{"en":"The invention of gunpowder was really an “accident”.","tok":[["火药","huǒyào","gunpowder","J"],["的","de"],["发明","fāmíng"],["其实","qíshí"],["是","shì"],["一","yī"],["个","gè"],"“",["意外","yìwài"],"”","。"]},{"en":"In ancient times some Daoists tried to produce an elixir that would let whoever took it live forever.","tok":[["古代","gǔdài"],["有","yǒu"],["一些","yīxiē"],["道士","dàoshì","Daoist priest","J"],["想","xiǎng"],["炼","liàn","to refine by heating"],["出","chū"],["一","yī"],["种","zhǒng"],["吃","chī"],["了","le"],["以后","yǐhòu"],["能","néng"],["长生不老","chángshēng bùlǎo","to live forever","I"],["的","de"],["药","yào"],"。"]},{"en":"They heated all kinds of substances in their furnaces, among them saltpetre, sulphur and charcoal.","tok":[["他们","tāmen"],["把","bǎ"],["各种","gèzhǒng"],["东西","dōngxi"],["放","fàng"],["在","zài"],["炉子","lúzi","furnace, stove"],["里","lǐ"],["加热","jiārè","to heat"],"，",["其中","qízhōng"],["就","jiù"],["有","yǒu"],["硝石","xiāoshí","saltpetre","J"],"、",["硫磺","liúhuáng","sulphur","J"],["和","hé"],["木炭","mùtàn","charcoal","J"],"。"]},{"en":"They found that when these three were mixed, a single spark made them suddenly burst into flame or even explode, sometimes burning down the building as well.","tok":[["他们","tāmen"],["发现","fāxiàn"],"，",["这","zhè"],["三","sān"],["种","zhǒng"],["东西","dōngxi"],["放","fàng"],["在","zài"],["一起","yīqǐ"],"，",["一","yī"],["点","diǎn"],["火","huǒ"],["就","jiù"],["会","huì"],["突然","tūrán"],["燃烧","ránshāo","to burn"],"，",["甚至","shènzhì"],["爆炸","bàozhà","to explode"],"，",["有时候","yǒushíhou"],["还","hái"],["会","huì"],["烧","shāo"],["坏","huài"],["房子","fángzi"],"。"]},{"en":"By about the Tang dynasty, books were already warning people to be careful with this dangerous mixture.","tok":[["大概","dàgài"],["在","zài"],["唐代","Tángdài","Tang dynasty (618–907)","N"],"，",["已经","yǐjīng"],["有","yǒu"],["书","shū"],["提醒","tíxǐng"],["人们","rénmen"],["要","yào"],["小心","xiǎoxīn"],["这种","zhèzhǒng"],["危险","wēixiǎn"],["的","de"],["混合物","hùnhéwù","mixture"],"。"]}],"zh":"火药的发明其实是一个“意外”。古代有一些道士想炼出一种吃了以后能长生不老的药。他们把各种东西放在炉子里加热，其中就有硝石、硫磺和木炭。他们发现，这三种东西放在一起，一点火就会突然燃烧，甚至爆炸，有时候还会烧坏房子。大概在唐代，已经有书提醒人们要小心这种危险的混合物。"}
{"type":"p","id":"gp-2","segs":[{"en":"The elixir of immortality was never achieved, but people soon found another use for gunpowder: war.","tok":[["长生不老","chángshēng bùlǎo","to live forever","I"],["的","de"],["药","yào"],["没有","méiyǒu"],["炼","liàn","to refine by heating"],["成","chéng"],"，",["人们","rénmen"],["却","què"],["很","hěn"],["快","kuài"],["发现","fāxiàn"],["了","le"],["火药","huǒyào","gunpowder","J"],["的","de"],["另","lìng","another"],["一","yī"],["个","gè"],["用处","yòngchu","use"],"：",["打仗","dǎzhàng","to fight a war"],"。"]},{"en":"Song armies used gunpowder to make fire arrows, fire balls and bombs.","tok":[["宋代","Sòngdài","Song dynasty","N"],["的","de"],["军队","jūnduì","army"],["用","yòng"],["火药","huǒyào","gunpowder","J"],["做成","zuòchéng"],["了","le"],["火箭","huǒjiàn","fire arrow (today: rocket)","J"],"、",["火球","huǒqiú","fire ball, incendiary ball","J"],["和","hé"],["炸弹","zhàdàn","bomb"],"。"]},{"en":"A military book from the Northern Song already recorded several gunpowder recipes in detail.","tok":[["北宋","Běi Sòng","Northern Song dynasty (960–1127)","N"],["时期","shíqī","period"],["的","de"],["一","yī"],["本","běn"],["军事","jūnshì","military"],["书","shū"],["里","lǐ"],"，",["已经","yǐjīng"],["详细","xiángxì","detailed"],["地","de"],["记录","jìlù"],["了","le"],["几","jǐ"],["种","zhǒng"],["火药","huǒyào","gunpowder","J"],["的","de"],["配方","pèifāng","recipe, formula"],"。"]},{"en":"Later, people made weapons that fired from bamboo tubes or metal barrels: these were the earliest guns and cannons.","tok":[["后来","hòulái"],"，",["人们","rénmen"],["又","yòu"],["做","zuò"],["出","chū"],["了","le"],["用","yòng"],["竹筒","zhútǒng","bamboo tube"],["或者","huòzhě"],["金属","jīnshǔ","metal"],["管子","guǎnzi","tube, pipe"],["发射","fāshè","to fire, to launch"],["的","de"],["武器","wǔqì","weapon"],"，",["这","zhè"],["就是","jiùshì"],["最","zuì"],["早","zǎo"],["的","de"],["枪","qiāng","gun"],["和","hé"],["炮","pào","cannon"],"。"]}],"zh":"长生不老的药没有炼成，人们却很快发现了火药的另一个用处：打仗。宋代的军队用火药做成了火箭、火球和炸弹。北宋时期的一本军事书里，已经详细地记录了几种火药的配方。后来，人们又做出了用竹筒或者金属管子发射的武器，这就是最早的枪和炮。"}
{"type":"p","id":"gp-3","segs":[{"en":"Gunpowder brought people joy as well, of course.","tok":[["当然","dāngrán"],"，",["火药","huǒyào","gunpowder","J"],["也","yě"],["给","gěi"],["人们","rénmen"],["带来","dàilái"],["了","le"],["快乐","kuàilè"],"。"]},{"en":"The firecrackers and fireworks set off at New Year are all made with gunpowder.","tok":[["过年","guònián"],["的","de"],["时候","shíhou"],["放","fàng"],["的","de"],["鞭炮","biānpào","firecrackers","J"],["和","hé"],["烟花","yānhuā","fireworks","J"],"，",["都","dōu"],["是","shì"],["用","yòng"],["火药","huǒyào","gunpowder","J"],["做","zuò"],["的","de"],"。"]},{"en":"Around the thirteenth century, gunpowder spread to the Middle East and Europe through the wars of the Mongols.","tok":[["大约","dàyuē"],["在","zài"],["十三","shísān"],["世纪","shìjì"],"，",["火药","huǒyào","gunpowder","J"],["通过","tōngguò"],["蒙古","Měnggǔ","Mongol, Mongolia","N"],["人","rén"],["的","de"],["战争","zhànzhēng"],["传","chuán"],["到","dào"],["了","le"],["中东","Zhōngdōng","Middle East","N"],["和","hé"],["欧洲","Ōuzhōu","Europe"],"。"]},{"en":"Once there were guns and cannons, the old city walls and iron armour became less and less useful, and the face of war changed completely.","tok":[["有","yǒu"],["了","le"],["枪","qiāng","gun"],["炮","pào","cannon"],["以后","yǐhòu"],"，",["以前","yǐqián"],["的","de"],["城墙","chéngqiáng","city wall"],["和","hé"],["铁甲","tiějiǎ","iron armour"],["越来越","yuèláiyuè"],["没用","méiyòng"],"，",["战争","zhànzhēng"],["的","de"],["样子","yàngzi"],["也","yě"],["完全","wánquán"],["改变","gǎibiàn"],["了","le"],"。"]}],"zh":"当然，火药也给人们带来了快乐。过年的时候放的鞭炮和烟花，都是用火药做的。大约在十三世纪，火药通过蒙古人的战争传到了中东和欧洲。有了枪炮以后，以前的城墙和铁甲越来越没用，战争的样子也完全改变了。"}
{"type":"h2","id":"h-end","segs":[{"en":"Not Just Four","tok":[["不只","bùzhǐ","not only"],["是","shì"],["四","sì"],["个","gè"]]}],"zh":"不只是四个"}
{"type":"p","id":"end-1","segs":[{"en":"Interestingly, the phrase “Four Great Inventions” does not go back to ancient times.","tok":[["有意思","yǒuyìsi"],["的","de"],["是","shì"],"，","“",["四大发明","sì dà fāmíng","Four Great Inventions","J"],"”",["这个","zhège"],["说法","shuōfǎ","expression, phrase"],["并","bìng"],["不","bù"],["是","shì"],["古代","gǔdài"],["就","jiù"],["有","yǒu"],["的","de"],"。"]},{"en":"Some four hundred years ago the English thinker Francis Bacon wrote that three inventions – printing, gunpowder and the compass – had changed the whole world; but he did not know that all three came from China.","tok":[["四百","sìbǎi"],["多","duō"],["年","nián"],["前","qián"],"，",["英国","Yīngguó"],["学者","xuézhě","scholar"],["培根","Péigēn","Francis Bacon (1561–1626)","N"],["写","xiě"],["过","guo"],"，",["印刷术","yìnshuāshù","printing","J"],"、",["火药","huǒyào","gunpowder","J"],["和","hé"],["指南针","zhǐnánzhēn","compass","J"],["这","zhè"],["三","sān"],["种","zhǒng"],["发明","fāmíng"],["改变","gǎibiàn"],["了","le"],["整个","zhěnggè"],["世界","shìjiè"],"，",["可是","kěshì"],["他","tā"],["并","bìng"],["不","bù"],["知道","zhīdào"],["它们","tāmen"],["都","dōu"],["来自","láizì"],["中国","Zhōngguó"],"。"]},{"en":"Later, Western scholars of Chinese history added papermaking to the list, and only in the twentieth century did “the Four Great Inventions” become a popular phrase.","tok":[["后来","hòulái"],"，",["研究","yánjiū"],["中国","Zhōngguó"],["历史","lìshǐ"],["的","de"],["西方","xīfāng"],["学者","xuézhě","scholar"],["把","bǎ"],["造纸术","zàozhǐshù","papermaking","J"],["也","yě"],["加","jiā"],["了","le"],["进去","jìnqù"],"，",["到","dào"],["了","le"],["二十","èrshí"],["世纪","shìjì"],"，","“",["四大发明","sì dà fāmíng","Four Great Inventions","J"],"”",["才","cái"],["成为","chéngwéi"],["一","yī"],["个","gè"],["流行","liúxíng"],["的","de"],["说法","shuōfǎ","expression, phrase"],"。"]}],"zh":"有意思的是，“四大发明”这个说法并不是古代就有的。四百多年前，英国学者培根写过，印刷术、火药和指南针这三种发明改变了整个世界，可是他并不知道它们都来自中国。后来，研究中国历史的西方学者把造纸术也加了进去，到了二十世纪，“四大发明”才成为一个流行的说法。"}
{"type":"p","id":"end-2","segs":[{"en":"In fact, ancient China invented far more than these four things.","tok":[["其实","qíshí"],"，",["中国","Zhōngguó"],["古代","gǔdài"],["的","de"],["发明","fāmíng"],["远远","yuǎnyuǎn","far (more)"],["不止","bùzhǐ","more than, not limited to"],["这","zhè"],["四","sì"],["个","gè"],"。"]},{"en":"Silk, porcelain, the abacus, paper money and Zhang Heng's seismoscope were all Chinese creations.","tok":[["丝绸","sīchóu","silk"],"、",["瓷器","cíqì","porcelain","J"],"、",["算盘","suànpán","abacus","J"],"、",["纸币","zhǐbì","paper money","J"],"，",["还有","háiyǒu"],["张衡","Zhāng Héng","Zhang Heng (78–139), Han astronomer","N"],["的","de"],["地动仪","dìdòngyí","seismoscope","J"],"，",["都","dōu"],["是","shì"],["中国","Zhōngguó"],["人","rén"],["的","de"],["创造","chuàngzào"],"。"]},{"en":"And a technology changes the world not only because it was invented, but because people in many different countries learned it, improved it and finally carried it to every part of the world.","tok":[["而且","érqiě"],"，",["一","yī"],["项","xiàng"],["技术","jìshù"],["能","néng"],["改变","gǎibiàn"],["世界","shìjiè"],"，",["不","bù"],["只","zhǐ"],["是","shì"],["因为","yīnwèi"],["它","tā"],["被","bèi"],["发明","fāmíng"],["了","le"],"，",["还","hái"],["因为","yīnwèi"],["很多","hěnduō"],["不同","bùtóng"],["国家","guójiā"],["的","de"],["人","rén"],["学习","xuéxí"],["它","tā"],"、",["改进","gǎijìn","to improve"],["它","tā"],"，",["最后","zuìhòu"],["把","bǎ"],["它","tā"],["带","dài"],["到","dào"],["了","le"],["世界","shìjiè"],["各","gè"],["地","dì"],"。"]},{"en":"The story of the Four Great Inventions is also a story of different cultures learning from one another.","tok":[["四大发明","sì dà fāmíng","Four Great Inventions","J"],["的","de"],["故事","gùshi"],"，",["也","yě"],["是","shì"],["不同","bùtóng"],["文化","wénhuà"],["互相","hùxiāng"],["学习","xuéxí"],["的","de"],["故事","gùshi"],"。"]}],"zh":"其实，中国古代的发明远远不止这四个。丝绸、瓷器、算盘、纸币，还有张衡的地动仪，都是中国人的创造。而且，一项技术能改变世界，不只是因为它被发明了，还因为很多不同国家的人学习它、改进它，最后把它带到了世界各地。四大发明的故事，也是不同文化互相学习的故事。"}
